{"id": "swebq0102", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.09, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3826, "eot_read_ms": 18, "reference_answer": "Pleistarchus", "query": "who was king after leonidas died?", "transcript": "Who was king after Leonidas died?", "mode": "local", "answer": "After Leonidas died, the Spartan army, led by King Leonnatus, continued to fight bravely at Thermopylae. However, Leonnatus was killed in battle. His death left a leadership gap, but the Spartans maintained their resolve. Ultimately, after the battle, the Spartan agoge system and existing political structures ensured that Spartan kingship continued, though specific succession details can vary depending on historical accounts.", "answer_ms": 1689}
